Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Bundles", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell["\<\
We start with a finite graph and a projection of its vertices. Equal fibers, \
lift existence, unique lifting and bundle structure are separate properties. \
Sections and complete connections add choices to this data.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a9a7af04-9244-4f2b-b4e7-9c82d3f38cd3"],

Cell["Topological language and finite readings", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3ea5a525-87b7-456b-8716-d98dd0d07a06"],

Cell["\<\
The finite object is a graph with a vertex projection. The following \
dictionary distinguishes its exact conditions from the additional structures \
of continuous topology.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2ae3a2a1-2ab9-4f1a-b98a-fcf51275db27"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "eba8ee4d-9b4e-449a-94af-fa40c6eb22e2"], Cell[
    "Topological notion", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"c62c4cea-5cde-4f20-a2f5-5839cb6071da"],
     Cell["Finite infra reading", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"71dade0f-61a6-49af-af44-47be3ec3dcc3"],
     Cell["Qualification", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"a4adc337-e39d-4341-be77-eefbb89c3d89"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "da84bdf2-b47e-4662-87a3-c49e877aad7f"], Cell[
    "Projection from total space to base", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "cdf54052-b75c-4a0b-a341-e4e06149ff3d"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberedGraph with InfraTotalSpace, InfraBaseSpace and InfraProjection\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"56b20424-aeba-47c9-b711-75c98aff45db"], 
    Cell["\<\
The base graph is reconstructed from projected edges; no topology is part of \
the inert object.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"819da838-e3ae-426f-a025-26b053aa03bf"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "a0b293a4-138e-45e0-a7f3-a752e2d4b820"], Cell[
    "Serre or Hurewicz fibration", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "52561b85-3017-48b9-8962-cc71595db7b9"], Cell["\<\
InfraFibrationQ asks for a lift of every base edge from every starting vertex\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"5f7d7eee-70c1-43ca-8159-5e8fcc00cfd3"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is weak edge-lift existence, not a homotopy-lifting axiom.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"2f97a16d-aa47-45ff-a5cd-3bf99c0ac7a7"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "ffcd6789-8cc4-4e06-9043-200719cb5c1e"], Cell[
    "Covering space", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "a2026015-5ff4-414e-9a81-1910091b72e2"], Cell["\<\
InfraCoveringQ gives edgeless fibers and a bijection on vertex neighbourhoods\
\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"832b0aed-fa9a-46ed-8ee5-40a11a718425"], 
    Cell["\<\
The graph-covering condition has the usual covering interpretation under \
graph realization. Sheet counts can differ across base components.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"9490d716-4b26-4466-839d-c2e8e3fc0f88"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "d848dece-e19f-4618-9806-7a1d38b4955e"], Cell[
    "Fiber bundle", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2f5bac85-7325-4576-a276-6f7d1761f135"], Cell["\<\
InfraFiberBundleQ gives a common fiber graph and adjacency-preserving \
transverse matchings\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"e5f90df6-920f-49fe-9e22-e7091f198fac"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is an edgewise Cartesian graph bundle. Realizing its edges alone does \
not supply topological product charts or filled squares.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"fefdc7b1-9bd9-407f-84fe-bef51d5c16f0"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "436643c1-71c3-47d1-ae2c-05eb36c5e2b1"], Cell[
    "Section", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "21764bf7-3b9c-487a-ba63-227eb4019054"], Cell[
    "InfraSection chooses a right inverse on a base domain", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"efc247a3-2f17-48c5-948c-e07ae851d87b"], Cell["\<\
InfraContinuousSectionQ asks for adjacency preservation on that domain.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ebd018cf-9ef3-433e-96a4-10a3c5040bcb"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "f6c59a3a-a6c7-462a-960e-9ce8b4433c21"], Cell[
    "Connection and parallel transport", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "1b3edae3-ffe1-4b55-aa00-524f733a2b59"], Cell["\<\
InfraConnection selects complete fiber matchings; transport composes them\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"df71a63d-b6cd-4b1b-abbc-784319bb1882"], 
    Cell["\<\
This is finite bijective transport. Preserving a fiber graph is an additional \
condition.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"43350af4-1b8a-4f0f-91fc-b795418f16c2"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "646caa5b-9d67-47ad-8d39-78b7e58fcce1"], Cell[
    "Infra-only transverse local conditions", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "71f23bef-f482-4b9a-bb7a-14d58532f86f"], Cell["\<\
InfraAtMostOneEdgeLiftQ and InfraFibrationQ read injectivity and surjectivity \
on transverse neighbours\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"ddf2d04d-2c56-49ad-9825-08bf65c6ef31"], 
    Cell["\<\
Vertical neighbours are excluded; the conditions do not assert local \
injectivity or surjectivity in a chosen topology.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"c2dacf39-3490-4bd1-9e0e-26572d9272d6"]},
   {Cell["      ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->
     "9f829db5-0120-4eaa-8df0-63605629f55d"], Cell[
    "Infra-only multiplicity and equitable partition", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"696d8479-adce-429c-bad5-1d9867c3ab90"], Cell["\<\
InfraEdgeLiftMultiplicity counts transverse neighbours, including zeros\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"399df04c-b600-4407-bc3a-5f0182e484b2"], 
    Cell["\<\
Constancy within each fiber is transverse equitability; full equitability \
also needs constant vertical degree.\
\>", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"392761e3-06cf-4a2c-a01a-eb92c2e41610"]}
  }]], "3ColumnTableMod",ExpressionUUID->"0002ebdf-70e7-489b-8277-\
0f1fd1a2e656"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For the continuous definitions, see ",
 ButtonBox["Hatcher, Algebraic Topology, Sections 1.3 and 4.2",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["https://pi.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/AT.pdf"], None}],
 ". The finite definitions and their implications are developed below."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a5e269d-de2f-42e4-a257-489eb8a4f8b1"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"130f8d4e-4e4d-494d-a81a-20dd62776644"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", " ", "\"\<WolframInstitute`InfraGeometry`\>\"", " ", 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"1ca7a03e-a1f6-463f-9a0b-727d5d683d8a"],

Cell["Total space, projection and fibers", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8eb34af2-eb2c-428b-8345-d3e72653d0cc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A ",
 StyleBox["fibered graph", "TI"],
 " consists of a finite simple undirected unweighted untagged graph ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["E", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "91f3c5d1-64a9-4057-b5d4-088afd9ee96c"],
 " and a map ",
 Cell[BoxData["\[Pi]"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9e6b7cf8-fdaf-4489-9790-c10e4055c21b"],
 " on its vertices. The ",
 StyleBox["base graph", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07ee7e47-b2d6-4b7f-827d-6a4e874e6a92"],
 " has vertex set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[Pi]", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["E", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8b9af073-ba02-474e-ba75-6fd31e66213c"],
 ". Distinct base vertices are adjacent exactly when some total edge joins \
their preimages. The ",
 StyleBox["fiber", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["F", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "17841fe1-1fd3-4514-8c29-d8b5eb0d36fe"],
 " is the induced graph on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", 
    RowBox[{"-", "1"}]], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1290d1d4-6db6-47fa-a831-b67397a19be6"],
 ". A total edge is ",
 StyleBox["vertical", "TI"],
 " when both endpoints project to the same vertex, and ",
 StyleBox["transverse", "TI"],
 " otherwise."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"445d4be6-34a3-41ad-b478-18d639a9ad18"],

Cell["\<\
The object carries no drawing, connection or lifting axiom. The base includes \
isolated projection values, and projection collapses vertical edges. The \
empty graph with empty projection is allowed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"63e3b23d-cb1e-4b10-812d-6f81bb2805f5"],

