Cell["\<\
Lift existence and at-most-one lifting together give unique lifting. Over a \
base edge, unique lifting gives a perfect matching: every vertex on either \
side has degree one. Consequently, fiber sizes agree within each connected \
base component. They need not agree between components.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57aa380b-d5b8-4375-aaa3-5e9761f8cfe8"],

Cell["\<\
Isomorphic fibers imply equal sizes, but impose no transverse-edge condition. \
A covering over a connected base is a bundle with a discrete fiber. A \
covering on a disconnected base may have different sheet counts and then \
lacks one common fiber.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"746fd1ac-a5b1-4ab3-9f62-6625ed094c23"],

Cell["\<\
These predicates treat the empty fibered graph vacuously. A nonempty list of \
objects is tested by conjunction; an empty list gives False. Malformed \
projections, unsupported graph domains and unknown construction heads remain \
unevaluated. Supported Experimental models have explicit predicate methods \
that materialize once; converting them to a literal object by hand is \
optional.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"abf2a17a-b296-44f5-a951-52e3f2d41f9d"],

Cell["Generate a prescribed class", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"890f1502-3167-46c2-b8db-2aa18a77e1d9"],

Cell["\<\
The generator retains every vertex and edge of the supplied base in the \
reconstructed base. Its default property list requests general fibered \
graphs. Properties are a flat conjunction of the conditions named in the \
symbol reference.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"170ab60d-23a9-4293-8f48-193f3248e5f0"],

